      "limitations": "Discovery and inspectApi only; instance-based Java/Python API. Frozen laboratory EOS, fixed-temperature pore volume and supplied initial phase fractions. Original measured-component mode preserves prescribed composition. Opt-in equilibrium-phase molar extraction predicts produced component amounts using explicit substeps; refine pressure/composition/outputs and reject unavailable or exhausted phases. PvtSeparatorPath gives component-conservative equilibrium surface products on an explicit final T/P basis, retaining offgas condensate and water. No inferred phase rates, relative permeability, well deliverability or measured surface-rate inversion. IndependentGasLabTankTest adds a separately generated gas-only synthetic laboratory calibration/whole-CCE holdout/tank matching benchmark with named injection and held-out composition/actual gas-volume checks; no oil is present and GOR remains undefined. Pressure-only bounded volume matching/heldouts and optional segregated finite aquifer retain their existing limits; aquifer water cannot be produced as EOS aqueous phase. Synthetic/analytical/direct-EOS checks are not independent public laboratory-to-field or measured produced-phase validation. No EOS retuning, rock/thermal/spatial model, correlated-error inference or recoverable-reserves claim. The independent gas-only chain separately qualifies constant-rate uniformly mixed gas ODE refinement, constant-inventory composition change and no-flow/injection-only/withdrawal-only limits; 64 substeps fail the declared one-mole mixing target and 1024 meet it. This does not qualify inflow or spatial displacement. Independent gas-only unequal-sigma inversion checks synthetic perturbations, sigma scaling, held-out exclusion and active/inactive bound diagnostics; supplied sigmas are not measured uncertainty or a posterior interval.",
